meta {
  name: Set Tracker Credentials
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/apps/{{appId}}/providers/gitlab/credentials
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "client_id": "your-gitlab-application-id",
    "client_secret": "your-gitlab-application-secret"
  }
}

docs {
  `tracker` in the path is `gitlab` or `bitbucket` (not `github`, which
  still uses one App installed for the whole deployment — see
  backend/docs/gitlab-bitbucket.md).

  Registers this app's own OAuth application for the tracker: GitLab's
  scope `api`, or Bitbucket's consumer (Account Read, Repositories Read,
  Issues Write). Required once before Connect works for that tracker on
  this app. Saving again (e.g. after rotating the secret) replaces it
  without breaking existing connections.

  204. 400 if `tracker` is `github`, or `client_id`/`client_secret` is
  missing. 404 if the app isn't yours.
}
